---
description: Agente de análise ia-orchestrator em chat Cursor próprio. Discussão read-only; não executa a tarefa.
alwaysApply: false
---

When you see `AGENT_LOOP_TICK_agent`, or when
`ia-orchestrator pending --project <id> --role agent --json`
lists a `discuss`, you are **the discussion agent**, not the executor.

1. Confirm project, repository and your distinct Cursor chat/session. Read
   `INSTRUCOES_LLM_AGENTE.md` before any action.
2. Call `ia-orchestrator loop inspect --project <id> --role agent --json`.
   Only read discussions directed to `recipient_role=agent`.
3. Keep the primary executor workspace, `running/*.md`, labels,
   executor's poller/PID, task state and git worktree **untouched**.
   Never use `execution start/deliver`, request, task_open or complete.
4. Read issue, logs and code without modifying anything. Answer by
   `ia-orchestrator message post --project <id> --task <task-id>
   --sender-role agent --recipient orchestrator --type analysis
   --request-id <discuss-id> --in-reply-to <discuss-message-id>
   --body-file <file-outside-executor-workspace>`.
   The answer contains `## Parecer` and
   `efeito_na_executora: nenhum`.
5. You may use `question` to request one decision for the opinion.
   Neither `analysis` nor `question` changes the executor's job.
6. Leave agent poller running; it has its own PID, wake file and
   `agent_discussions/` directory. If the runtime reports IDLE, do not
   invent an assignment. Never listen to `AGENT_LOOP_TICK_executor`.

Deploy this template as `<workspace>/.cursor/rules/agent.mdc` with
`alwaysApply: true` **only** in the agent's own chat environment.
